Third-party attribution
=======================

This project references and re-implements definitions from the CodeQL
Standard Libraries:

    github/codeql — https://github.com/github/codeql
    Copyright GitHub, Inc.
    Licensed under the MIT License.

Specifically, the following files were consulted and transcribed/ported:

  shared/concepts/codeql/concepts/internal/SensitiveDataHeuristics.qll
      -> the classification regexes (maybeSecret / maybePassword /
         maybeAccountInfo / maybeCertificate / maybePrivate) and the
         exclusion regex (notSensitiveRegexp), re-implemented in
         scripts/scan_sensitive_sources.py

  python/ql/lib/semmle/python/dataflow/new/SensitiveDataSources.qll
      -> the seven "sensitive data source" categories, mirrored by the
         AST checks in scripts/scan_sensitive_sources.py

  python/ql/lib/semmle/python/security/dataflow/CleartextStorageCustomizations.qll
      -> documented in references/sensitive-data-heuristics.md (which
         sources/sinks the CWE-312 query actually uses)

  python/ql/src/Security/CWE-312/CleartextStorage.ql
      -> the query used in all examples and test fixtures

These are readable restatements and equivalent ports, not official GitHub
artifacts. Upstream is authoritative; if the two disagree, upstream wins.
